From 78a451dd07ed4c107c096af25a37c23c48ecfe1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Vicory <dvicory@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 23:55:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): harden lifecycle and separate orchestration authority

Rejected completion must leave a worker responsible for reaching a real
terminal state, and repeated unblock/re-block cycles must escalate instead of
looping forever.  Live board sessions also need different authority from a
dispatcher-assigned worker: sharing one guidance block and lifecycle tool gate
allowed the live model to complete or block tasks it did not own.

Preserve rejected-completion recovery, count recurring blockers, select the
role contract from HERMES_KANBAN_TASK, and reserve complete, block, and
heartbeat tools for assigned workers.  This patch is backend-independent and
should survive Hermes upgrades regardless of the execution or workspace
backend.
---
